{
  "slug": "intention-driven-design",
  "name": "Intention Driven Design",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Intention-Driven Design (IDD) is a methodology for building software where every artifact traces back to a declared human intent. Code is a downstream consequence of intent, never the starting point. We allow change, but we do not allow drift.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `behavior-contract` (Convert solution narratives into BDD feature files and protocol contracts), `certification` (Verify traceability and produce evidence that implementation fulfills declared intent), `domain-modeling` (Define domain entities, value objects, aggregates, and business rules), `e2e-journey-testing` (End-to-end test development from user journeys), `idd-workflow` (Meta-skill explaining when to use each development skill), `pr-review` (Verify IDD compliance on pull requests), `solution-narrative` (User journey and story development)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install intention-driven-design@claude-community` from `slusset/intention-driven-design`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
